Question: Which NYC airport has the longest average departure delay?
Pseudocode: group flights by origin airport → average the departure delay in each group (skip NAs for cancelled flights) → count flights per group for context → sort, biggest first.

flights |&gt;
  group_by(origin) |&gt;
  summarize(
    avg_dep_delay = mean(dep_delay, na.rm = TRUE),
    n_flights = n()
  ) |&gt;
  arrange(desc(avg_dep_delay))

# A tibble: 3 × 3
  origin avg_dep_delay n_flights
  &lt;chr&gt;          &lt;dbl&gt;     &lt;int&gt;
1 EWR             15.1    120835
2 JFK             12.1    111279
3 LGA             10.3    104662


Answer: Newark (EWR) has the longest average departure delay at 15.1 minutes, followed by JFK (12.1) and LaGuardia (10.3).
